HTML:

Update the <title> tag by changing [Your Name] to your name.



In the <head> tag, link your CSS file to your HTML file.

<link href="style.css" rel="stylesheet" />



In the <body> tag, add a <div> tag with an ID of "info". Don't forget to close your tags.

<div id="info">	</div>



Within that <div> tag with the "info", add an H1 tag with "About" as the content, add a H2 tag with "[Your Name]", add a H3 tag with "[Your Title]".

<div id="info">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <h2>Brenna Tichy</h2>
    <h3>Student Journalist</h3>
</div>



Below your H3 tag, add your headshot to the HTML using <img src="">.

<img src="IMG_3140.jpeg">



Give the image tag a alt attribute.

<img src="IMG_3140.jpeg" alt="Headshot of Brenna Tichy" />



Give the image tag the ID of "headshot."

<img src="IMG_3140.jpeg" alt="Headshot of Brenna Tichy" id="headshot" />



Below the image, put a description of you in a <p> tag. Begin your description with "[Your Name] is"

<p>Brenna Tichy is an editorial intern at Baltimore Magazine</p>



Below that description, add a <div> tag with an ID of contact.

<div id="contact"></div>



Put "Contact me" in that <div> tag, link it to your email address.

<div id="contact">
    <a href="mailto:btichy@terpmail.umd.edu">Contact me</a>
</div>



Below the entire "info" <div> tag, add a <div> tag with an ID of "footer". In that tag put: Copyright 2026 [Your Name].

<div id="footer">
    Copyright 2026 Brenna Tichy
</div>





CSS:

Make your headshot 300px wide. (Use the element's ID as the selector.)

#headshot {
    width: 300px;
}



Make the font of everything in the body of your HTML the following: "Arial,   sans-serif".

body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}



Make the "Contact Me" font bold, black, and 20px big. (You will need to use a selector that targets the "a" tag after the "contact" div. Make it turn red on hover. (Helpful link: CSS Selectors Links to an external site.)

#contact a {
    font-weight: bold;
    color: black;
    font-size:20px;
}


#contact a:hover {
    color:red;
}



Make your "info" div 500px wide. Center your "info" div by adding the following declaration: margin:auto

#info {
    width:500px;
    margin:auto;
}



Float your headshot to the left of your description and "Contact Me" link.

#headshot {
    width: 300px;
    float:left;
    margin-right:10px;
}


Adjust the margins on your elements to create space between your image and text.

#headshot {
    width: 300px;
    float: left;
    margin-right: 10px;
}



Use media queries to make it so your "info" is 100% and your headshot is stacked above your description on any device under 576px.

At Top:
@media screen {
    #headshot {
        width: 100%;
        float: none;
    }
}

At Bottom:
@media (min-width: 576px) {
    #headshot {
        width: 300px;
        float: left;
        margin-right: 10px;
    }
}



Fix your footer at the bottom of your page using the "position" and "bottom" property. It will also need a background color, padding, and width.
    
#footer {
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 0px;
    left: 0px;
    background-color: lightblue;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 10px;
}


